                                       VPC
                             Virtual Private Cloud

--> VPC is a virtual network or data center for one client
--> it is logically isolated from other virtual betwork in the AWWS Cloud
--> once we created VPC, DHCP, security group and NACL will be automatically created
DHCP: Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol

--> VPC types:
1. Default VPC
2. Custom VPC

--> up to 5 VPC you can create per region and 200 subnets in 1 VPC
--> once the VPC is created, ypu can not chnaged its CIDR block
--> if you need differnt CIDR size, then create new VPC
--> different subnet within a VPC can not overlap

--> steps to create VPC:
1. create VPC  
    -----> 1. VPC name
    -----> 2. VPC CIDR --> 10.0.0.0/16 ---> 65536

2. create subnet
--> subnet means sub network
--> subnet is a range of an ip address
--> subnetting --> is the process of dividing large network into smaller one
--> why?? 
    ---> can help to reduce the congesion
    ---> better IP allocation
    ---> better security

-----------> 1. subnet name
-----------> 2. Subnet CIDR --> 10.0.0.0/20

3. Internet Gateway
--> gateway is used to connect two different network
--> An internet gateway is a virtual router that connects a VPC to the internet. 

4. Route table
----> to select subnet association
----> enter routes
